---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const portraitSrc = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/portrait.jpg`;
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Homepage identity POC — round two | Steven Chu"
	description="Three refined name-led homepage identity directions for local portfolio review."
>
	<main class="poc" data-poc-root data-show-status="true" data-show-experience="true">
		<header class="review-header wrapper">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Exploratory · Issue #22 · Round two</p>
				<h1>Name first. Role second. Proof after.</h1>
				<p class="intro">
					Three narrowed directions based on the first review. All keep Steven’s name as the dominant
					first-scan element and treat Staff positioning as context rather than the main message.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="review-notes">
				<strong>Review for</strong>
				<span>one clear entry point</span>
				<span>20-second recognition</span>
				<span>humanity without duplication</span>
			</div>
		</header>

		<section class="controls wrapper" aria-label="Prototype controls">
			<div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Round-two concepts">
				<button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-concept-target="a">
					A · Name + profile + powers
				</button>
				<button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-concept-target="b">
					B · Name + thesis + powers
				</button>
				<button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-concept-target="c">
					C · Name + role + proof
				</button>
			</div>

			<fieldset class="toggles">
				<legend>Signals</legend>
				<label><input type="checkbox" data-feature-toggle="status" checked /> Availability</label>
				<label><input type="checkbox" data-feature-toggle="experience" checked /> Experience strip</label>
			</fieldset>
		</section>

		<div class="stage">
			<section class="panel" role="tabpanel" data-concept="a" aria-labelledby="concept-a-title">
				<div class="canvas wrapper">
					<div class="utility-row">
						<p class="role-line">Staff Product Designer · New York</p>
						<span class="status" data-feature="status">Open to select opportunities</span>
					</div>

					<div class="name-profile-grid">
						<h2 id="concept-a-title" class="display-name">Steven Chu</h2>

						<div class="profile-note">
							<img src={portraitSrc} width="176" height="176" alt="Steven Chu smiling" />
							<p>
								A systems-minded product builder with visual craft, front-end fluency, and a
								teacher’s attention to how people enter unfamiliar experiences.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="powers powers-three">
						<article>
							<span>01</span>
							<h3>Systems that adapt</h3>
							<p>
								I create shared foundations that support meaningful variation without turning into
								separate products.
							</p>
						</article>
						<article>
							<span>02</span>
							<h3>Strategy to software</h3>
							<p>
								I use front-end and AI-assisted building to test product judgment in working
								experiences.
							</p>
						</article>
						<article>
							<span>03</span>
							<h3>Better ways to make</h3>
							<p>
								I redesign systems and workflows so teams can ship consistently without flattening
								the craft.
							</p>
						</article>
					</div>

					<div class="secondary-practice">
						<p class="eyebrow">Teaching and community</p>
						<p>
							Open-level pole classes and intergenerational queer tech programs keep me attentive
							to participation, feedback, confidence, and multiple ways of learning.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="experience-strip" data-feature="experience" aria-label="Selected experience">
						<p class="eyebrow">Selected experience</p>
						<ul>
							<li>BOSE</li>
							<li>UNIQLO</li>
							<li>Motif</li>
							<li>STATE FARM</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>

				<aside class="rationale wrapper">
					<div>
						<p class="eyebrow">Why this fixes 3 + 4</p>
						<p>
							There is one identity entry point: the name. The profile block explains how Steven
							operates without introducing him a second time. Three professional powers carry the
							main evidence; teaching becomes a quieter reinforcing practice.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<p class="eyebrow">Watch for</p>
						<p>
							The right profile block still needs to feel necessary. If it reads as a second hero,
							Concept B is cleaner.
						</p>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</section>

			<section class="panel" role="tabpanel" data-concept="b" aria-labelledby="concept-b-title" hidden>
				<div class="canvas wrapper">
					<div class="utility-row">
						<p class="role-line">New York-based Staff Product Designer</p>
						<span class="status" data-feature="status">Open to select opportunities</span>
					</div>

					<div class="name-portrait-grid">
						<div>
							<h2 id="concept-b-title" class="display-name">I’m Steven.</h2>
							<p class="hero-thesis">
								I design products and the systems around them—from platform logic and interaction
								design through visual craft and working front-end prototypes.
							</p>
						</div>

						<img
							class="portrait-medium"
							src={portraitSrc}
							width="420"
							height="540"
							alt="Steven Chu smiling in a white shirt and custom overalls"
						/>
					</div>

					<div class="powers powers-three">
						<article>
							<span>01</span>
							<h3>Systems that adapt</h3>
							<p>Shared foundations that preserve meaningful variation without fragmentation.</p>
						</article>
						<article>
							<span>02</span>
							<h3>Strategy to software</h3>
							<p>Working prototypes that expose product decisions earlier and more honestly.</p>
						</article>
						<article>
							<span>03</span>
							<h3>Better ways to make</h3>
							<p>Systems and workflows that increase consistency without removing the craft.</p>
						</article>
					</div>

					<div class="community-bridge">
						<strong>I also teach and build community.</strong>
						<span>
							Pole instruction and intergenerational LGBTQ+ storytelling keep my design practice
							grounded in how people learn, participate, and gain confidence.
						</span>
					</div>

					<div class="experience-strip" data-feature="experience" aria-label="Selected experience">
						<p class="eyebrow">Selected experience</p>
						<ul>
							<li>BOSE</li>
							<li>UNIQLO</li>
							<li>Motif</li>
							<li>STATE FARM</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>

				<aside class="rationale wrapper">
					<div>
						<p class="eyebrow">Why it may be strongest</p>
						<p>
							This has the cleanest information flow: identity, one professional thesis, three
							proof categories, then a secondary human signal. The portrait supports recognition
							without becoming a separate biography block.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<p class="eyebrow">Watch for</p>
						<p>
							The introduction is more controlled than Taamannae’s and may feel less conversational.
							The final copy will need a little warmth without adding another text layer.
						</p>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</section>

			<section class="panel" role="tabpanel" data-concept="c" aria-labelledby="concept-c-title" hidden>
				<div class="canvas wrapper">
					<div class="utility-row">
						<p class="role-line">Staff Product Designer · New York</p>
						<span class="status" data-feature="status">Open to select opportunities</span>
					</div>

					<div class="fallback-grid">
						<div>
							<h2 id="concept-c-title" class="display-name">Steven Chu</h2>
							<p class="hero-thesis">
								I combine systems rigor, visual craft, front-end fluency, and a teacher’s
								perspective to shape accessible products that help people create, build skills, and
								access valuable services.
							</p>
						</div>

						<img
							class="portrait-fallback"
							src={portraitSrc}
							width="420"
							height="540"
							alt="Steven Chu smiling in a white shirt and custom overalls"
						/>
					</div>

					<div class="proof-row">
						<article>
							<strong>10+ years</strong>
							<span>Across product development, enterprise platforms, and design systems</span>
						</article>
						<article>
							<strong>1,300+ institutions</strong>
							<span>Accessible theming logic for one shared financial platform</span>
						</article>
						<article>
							<strong>Builder since age 12</strong>
							<span>From custom websites to independently launched working products</span>
						</article>
					</div>

					<div class="experience-strip prominent" data-feature="experience" aria-label="Selected experience">
						<p class="eyebrow">Selected experience</p>
						<ul>
							<li>BOSE</li>
							<li>UNIQLO</li>
							<li>Motif</li>
							<li>STATE FARM</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>

				<aside class="rationale wrapper">
					<div>
						<p class="eyebrow">Why it is the fallback</p>
						<p>
							It retains Concept 1’s recruiter clarity while correcting the emphasis: the name is
							the headline, the role is metadata, and proof is organized in one restrained row.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<p class="eyebrow">Watch for</p>
						<p>
							This is credible and easy to process, but it says less about your personality and
							operating style than A or B.
						</p>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</section>
		</div>
	</main>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
	const root = document.querySelector('[data-poc-root]');
	const tabs = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[data-concept-target]'));
	const panels = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[data-concept]'));
	const toggles = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[data-feature-toggle]'));

	const activateConcept = (concept) => {
		tabs.forEach((tab) => {
			const selected = tab.getAttribute('data-concept-target') === concept;
			tab.setAttribute('aria-selected', selected ? 'true' : 'false');
		});

		panels.forEach((panel) => {
			panel.hidden = panel.getAttribute('data-concept') !== concept;
		});

		history.replaceState(null, '', `#concept-${concept}`);
	};

	tabs.forEach((tab) => {
		tab.addEventListener('click', () => activateConcept(tab.getAttribute('data-concept-target') || 'a'));
	});

	toggles.forEach((toggle) => {
		toggle.addEventListener('change', () => {
			const feature = toggle.getAttribute('data-feature-toggle');
			if (root && feature) root.setAttribute(`data-show-${feature}`, toggle.checked ? 'true' : 'false');
		});
	});

	const initial = window.location.hash.match(/concept-([abc])/)?.[1];
	if (initial) activateConcept(initial);
</script>

<style>
	.poc {
		--poc-max: 82rem;
		padding-bottom: 8rem;
	}

	.poc[data-show-status='false'] [data-feature='status'],
	.poc[data-show-experience='false'] [data-feature='experience'] {
		display: none;
	}

	.wrapper {
		width: min(calc(100% - 2rem), var(--poc-max));
		margin-inline: auto;
	}

	.review-header {
		display: grid;
		gap: 2rem;
		padding-block: 4rem 2rem;
	}

	.review-header h1 {
		max-width: 17ch;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5.6rem);
		font-weight: var(--weight-display);
		line-height: 0.98;
		letter-spacing: -0.05em;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.intro {
		max-width: 64ch;
		margin-top: 1.25rem;
		font-size: var(--role-subhead-size);
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
	}

	.eyebrow,
	.role-line {
		font-size: var(--role-eyebrow-size);
		font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
		line-height: 1.4;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--text-tertiary);
	}

	.review-notes {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
		font-size: var(--role-meta-size);
		color: var(--text-secondary);
	}

	.review-notes strong {
		color: var(--text-primary);
	}

	.controls {
		position: sticky;
		top: 0;
		z-index: 20;
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding-block: 1rem;
		border-block: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface-page) 90%, transparent);
		backdrop-filter: blur(18px);
	}

	.tabs {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		overflow-x: auto;
	}

	.tabs button {
		flex: 0 0 auto;
		border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
		border-radius: 999px;
		padding: 0.65rem 1rem;
		background: var(--surface-page);
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		font: inherit;
		font-size: var(--role-meta-size);
		cursor: pointer;
	}

	.tabs button[aria-selected='true'] {
		border-color: var(--text-primary);
		background: var(--text-primary);
		color: var(--surface-page);
	}

	.toggles {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
		border: 0;
		padding: 0;
		font-size: var(--role-meta-size);
		color: var(--text-secondary);
	}

	.toggles legend {
		float: left;
		margin-right: 1rem;
		font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
		color: var(--text-primary);
	}

	.toggles label {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.4rem;
	}

	.stage {
		padding-top: 3rem;
	}

	.canvas {
		padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 8rem);
	}

	.utility-row {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 1rem;
		margin-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem);
	}

	.status {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.65rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
		border-radius: 999px;
		padding: 0.7rem 1rem;
		font-size: var(--role-body-size);
		color: var(--text-secondary);
	}

	.status::before {
		content: '';
		inline-size: 0.5rem;
		block-size: 0.5rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: currentColor;
	}

	.display-name {
		max-width: 8ch;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: clamp(4.8rem, 14vw, 11rem);
		font-weight: var(--weight-display);
		line-height: 0.86;
		letter-spacing: -0.065em;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.name-profile-grid,
	.name-portrait-grid,
	.fallback-grid {
		display: grid;
		gap: 3rem;
		align-items: start;
	}

	.profile-note {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.25rem;
		align-content: start;
		max-width: 30rem;
	}

	.profile-note img {
		inline-size: 8.5rem;
		aspect-ratio: 1;
		object-fit: cover;
		object-position: top;
		border-radius: 50%;
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
	}

	.profile-note p,
	.hero-thesis {
		font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.3vw, 2rem);
		line-height: 1.45;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
	}

	.hero-thesis {
		max-width: 44ch;
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	.portrait-medium,
	.portrait-fallback {
		width: min(100%, 25rem);
		aspect-ratio: 3 / 4;
		object-fit: cover;
		object-position: top;
		border-radius: 2rem;
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
	}

	.powers {
		display: grid;
		margin-top: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
		border-block: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
	}

	.powers article {
		display: grid;
		align-content: start;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding-block: 2rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
	}

	.powers article:first-child {
		border-top: 0;
	}

	.powers article > span {
		font-size: var(--role-meta-size);
		color: var(--text-tertiary);
	}

	.powers h3 {
		max-width: 13ch;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
		font-weight: var(--weight-heading);
		line-height: 1.05;
		letter-spacing: -0.035em;
	}

	.powers p {
		max-width: 34ch;
		font-size: var(--role-body-size);
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
	}

	.secondary-practice,
	.community-bridge {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		max-width: 58rem;
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
		padding-top: 2rem;
	}

	.secondary-practice > p:last-child,
	.community-bridge span {
		font-size: var(--role-body-size);
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
	}

	.community-bridge strong {
		font-size: var(--role-heading-size);
	}

	.experience-strip {
		margin-top: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
		padding-block: 2rem;
		border-block: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
	}

	.experience-strip ul {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 1.5rem 2rem;
		margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}

	.experience-strip li {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 3.4rem);
		font-weight: var(--weight-heading);
		line-height: 1;
		letter-spacing: -0.035em;
		color: var(--text-primary);
	}

	.proof-row {
		display: grid;
		margin-top: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
		border-block: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
	}

	.proof-row article {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		padding-block: 1.75rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
	}

	.proof-row article:first-child {
		border-top: 0;
	}

	.proof-row strong {
		font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.4rem);
		line-height: 1.05;
	}

	.proof-row span {
		font-size: var(--role-body-size);
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
	}

	.rationale {
		display: grid;
		gap: 2rem;
		padding-block: 2rem 4rem;
		border-top: 1px dashed var(--border-strong);
	}

	.rationale > div {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.rationale p:last-child {
		max-width: 62ch;
		font-size: var(--role-body-size);
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
	}

	@media (min-width: 52em) {
		.review-header {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
			align-items: end;
			padding-block: 6rem 3rem;
		}

		.controls {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
			align-items: center;
		}

		.name-profile-grid {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.8fr) minmax(18rem, 0.75fr);
			gap: 5rem;
		}

		.name-portrait-grid,
		.fallback-grid {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.65fr) minmax(18rem, 0.65fr);
			gap: 5rem;
			align-items: center;
		}

		.powers-three,
		.proof-row {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
		}

		.powers article,
		.proof-row article {
			padding: 2.5rem 2rem;
			border-top: 0;
			border-left: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
		}

		.powers article:first-child,
		.proof-row article:first-child {
			padding-left: 0;
			border-left: 0;
		}

		.powers article:last-child,
		.proof-row article:last-child {
			padding-right: 0;
		}

		.experience-strip ul {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
			align-items: center;
		}

		.rationale {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
			gap: 4rem;
		}
	}
</style>
